    {
      "name": "Circuitborn: Firmware of Identity",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/melee/blade-tip-acid-poison-green.webp",
      "system": {
        "category": "technique",
        "source": {
          "custom": "Bad Eden",
          "rules": "2024",
          "revision": 1
        },
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "\n<p><em>“You are not a robot. You are a decision the world keeps making about itself.”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Firmware of Identity.</strong> You do not eat, drink, or sleep. You enter <em>maintenance trance</em> when you rest. You reroll the lowest die on checks against poison and disease, and you are immune to magical sleep.</p>\n<p><strong>Attention Resonance.</strong> 1/Soma Break, when a creature you can see is intensely focused on you (ally or enemy; GM adjudicates), you may regain either (a) 10 marks you spent this scene or (b) Integrity equal to your tier.</p>\n<p><strong>Informational Matrix Sense.</strong> You can feel active networks: radio, signal, ritual, rumor. You reroll the lowest die on checks to identify surveillance, hidden speakers, encoded messages, or noospheric “attention traps.”</p>\n<p><strong>Glitch-Surge.</strong> When you drop to 0 Integrity, you can choose to emit a controlled burst of static (no damage, but loud and disorienting) before you fall.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
